                <pb facs="0139" n="74" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg74"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/4308: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-07T11:00:00+03:00">May 7, 1936—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 7—10:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>305. Detachment of about 50 French Senegalese troops arrived yesterday from
                    Djibouti to guard railway station but left today as no longer needed. Five
                    hundred have been at Diré Dawa for several days and have received instructions
                    to prevent all rioting when Ethiopian authorities depart. Harrar is expected to
                    be in Italian hands in a day or two.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
